text Morning.
text I've been awake for a bit, but I'm just lazing around in my bed.
text I wonder if Furukawa's fever has gotten any better.
text Is she waiting for me on the path to school again?
text But what happened this weekend drove a bit of a wedge between the two of us.
text If I can feel it, then I'm certain she can too. She's even more perceptive than I am when it comes to relationship stuff.
text She worked hard for two days, but all she accomplished was to hurt someone else.
text Once she realized that, she called herself stupid.
text And what did I say in reply?
text @[Tomoya]
text ("You really are an idiot...")
text It'd be one thing if she was thick-skinned, but...
text She's unusually delicate about these things.
text In the end, I was no different from all her other classmates that do nothing but hurt her.
text She must have realized that too.
text ...I'll go to school once it's noon.
text After making the decision, I bury my face back into my futon.
