text I take a casual glance out the window.
text I see nothing but contrasting blues and greens at first, then I move my eyes down.
text She's there.
text @[Tomoya]
text (Furukawa...)
text @[Tomoya]
text (You came...)
text She's eating some bread in a way that I can only describe as vigorously.
text ...It's just like the first time I saw her.
text @[Tomoya]
text (...)
text Last week, I was down there next to her.
text But now I'm on the side of those students who look down at her.
sound H3A.aac
text @[Sunohara]
text Hey, Okazaki. Let's hurry. Lunch is gonna end.
text I hear Sunohara's voice.
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, yeah.
text Just then, Furukawa notices me.
text I wonder if she can tell that it's me.
text She takes the bread away from her mouth and puts it on top of her lap.
text She's gazing in my direction with a face that looks like it's on the verge of tears.
text I wonder if she's thinking about Saturday...
text She shifts her eyes down to the ground.
text @[Tomoya]
text (Furukawa...)
text I should leave. I can tell she doesn't want to see me for any longer than she already has.
text And yet, I can't move.
text Sunohara keeps on calling out to me.
text But... I just stay there.
music ~
text ......
text Furukawa peers back up again.
text And then...
text She raises a hand...
music BGM02A.mp3
text And waves it in my direction.
text She's making an effort to smile at me.
text ......
text ...I want to repay her.
text For putting everything she can into making herself do that.
text If she still needs me, that is.
